  "hypothesis": "A continuous 4x increase from 128 to 512 learning hands per opponent-seat group will improve reliability-shrunk frozen policy performance in at least two of three independent seeds while retaining nonnegative median final holdout and seat deltas, positive correct-versus-wrong context value, MGDA geometry, and Standard10 preservation.",
  "material_change": "Train three new posterior-centered seeds with one 64-hand warmup per each of twelve opponent-seat groups. Continue the same model, optimizer, and exact context counts through 128 then 512 learning hands/group, using 32 then 96 MGDA steps and fixed batch32. Freeze both endpoints and evaluate reliability-power1 execution on fresh nine-policy, both-seat, base/correct/wrong common decks.",
